<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kan Maax</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 800</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kan Maax was the last known king of the Maya city of Cancuén in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taj-chan-ahk">Taj Chan Ahk</a>. Around 800 he, his queen and about thirty nobles were killed and their bodies placed in a palace cistern, after which the city was abandoned. The massacre site, excavated in 2005, is vivid evidence of the violence of the Classic Maya collapse.</p></div>
